.TH GIT-MIRROR.SH 1 "2026-04-25" "GitMirror" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-mirror.sh \- mirror public GitHub repositories into a Gitea account
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bash git-mirror.sh
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-mirror.sh
reads settings from
.B config.json
and creates mirror repositories in Gitea using the Gitea migration API.
.PP
For each configured GitHub user, the script:
.IP "-"
Fetches public repositories from GitHub (paged requests).
.IP "-"
Skips repositories marked as forks.
.IP "-"
Skips repositories listed in
.B GH_EXCLUDE_REPOS
.
.IP "-"
Skips repositories that already exist in the target Gitea account.
.IP "-"
Creates mirror repositories for remaining entries.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The following keys are read from
.B config.json
:
.TP
.B GH_USERS
Array of GitHub users/organizations to scan.
.TP
.B GH_EXCLUDE_REPOS
Optional array of repository URLs to exclude.
.TP
.B GITEA_URL
Base URL of the Gitea instance.
.TP
.B GITEA_USER
Gitea username (may be required by related scripts).
.TP
.B GITEA_TOKEN
Gitea API token with permission to create repositories.
.SH OPTIONS
This command has no options.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B config.json
Required configuration file in the current working directory.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 on normal completion. Returns 2 for missing configuration or missing prerequisites.
.SH EXAMPLES
Mirror configured GitHub users into configured Gitea account:
.PP
.B bash git-mirror.sh
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-mirror-ghtest.sh (1),
.BR gitea-sync-all.sh (1),
.BR gitea-prune-orphans.sh (1)
